A||||21||Brandon86SE||Speeding Ticket||||8||
Z||000000||Brandon86SE||09-22-2001||07:48 PM||||Ok, here's the story:<P>I was driving Northbound on Deerfoot Trail (technically a provincial highway, not a city street) on my way to work this morning.  I was in the far right hand lane travelling around 100-105, the limit in the area is 100.  There is a blue Impala in front of me.  The lane I was in is essentially an extended merge lane, that ended about a kilometer ahead of where I was when I changed lanes into the second from the left.  The Impala was going between 90-100, so I slowly gained on him once over.  There was only a couple hundred metres left in the merge lane he was in, and I was right beside him, slowly overtaking him.  At this point I decided to be courteous and speed up a little to give him room to merge in behind me.  He did, and turned on his flashers (unmarked, ghost cop-car).  I pulled over, rolled down my window, took my seat belt off, and got my wallet out.  The cop walked up and said:  "You're getting a ticket for speeding, tail-gating, and not wearing a seatbelt."  At this I was stunned!  I explained to him how I just took the seatbelt off so as to get at my wallet, to which he kinda shrugged and grunted.  I gave him my license and registration, and while he was looking at that I inquired to his allegations of tailgating.  He said I was right behind the car in the lane I had pulled over to.  (When I sped up I got closer to a car that was about 7-8 car lenghts ahead of me).  I told him that I only sped up so that he would have room to merge.  To this he said: "I'll be back in a minute", and walked back to his patroller.  After a couple minutes he came back with my license, and gave me a ticket for doing 120 in a 100 zone (btw, everyone in the fast lane at the same time as this was doing about 120, that's the expected speed to be in the left lane).  So, anyway, he didn't give me a ticket for tailgating, or not wearing a seatbelt, but I'm still stuck with an $82 speeding ticket.<P>However, while on break at work, I was looking at the ticket, and realized that he was a city police officer, not RCMP.  If you're pulled over on Deerfoot, or 16th, doesn't it have to be by RC?  I'm pretty sure the highways through the city are outside of city cops jurisdiction.<P>Anyway, I'm planning on going to my court date in a month and explaining to the judge the situation, and exactly what happened.<P>If anyone knows about the jurisdiciton thing, it'd be great to hear.  Anyway, for now, I'm going to continue venting.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Neal||09-22-2001||07:58 PM||||Brandon, crappy luck.<P>and unfortunatly the cop does have the right to give you that ticket.  however sounds like a prick of a cop, and usually you can get tickets reduced just by showing up but in your case id fight it to the bitter end.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Capt Fiero||09-22-2001||08:21 PM||||I dont know where you are, but here in BC a buddy of mine got a ticket for racing in the industrial zone 1.5 years ago , he did not argue with the cop just took the ticket and left. He then waited till the last day to dispute the ticket, he faxed and mailed the dispute, then 8 months later he got a court date, that court date was 6 monthns from then.  So over a year for all this to happen.  When he got to court a few weeks ago, he pleaded not guilty due to lenght of time (some legal jargon I dont remember) and they waived the ticket and he got off scott free.  (400$ ticket plus 6 points on his lisc.) If for no other reason to fight it but give yourself 14 months to pay it off, just toss a quarter in a jar a day and then pay it. (LOL) ||||reg||1
Z||000003||crzyone||09-23-2001||12:10 AM||||That sucks man, sounds like he was having a bad day.  Seems there are alot of cops handing out tickets lately, they must have a quota to meet or something.  I travel highway 2 all the time and I've seen alot of people pulled over.  I would definitly take it to court, I'd say theres a good chance the cop won't even show up to court for such a small offence.<BR>Good Luck.<P>------------------<BR>86 GT 4 speed<BR>85 SC 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||09-23-2001||02:50 AM||||Hey Brandon!<BR>First off, if you are under 30 years old and a male driver, cops look for you...<BR>And seeing it is getting to the end of the month, it is quota time...<BR>Also, his wife has PMS and he hasn't been laid in 2 weeks...<BR>Plus you are driving a sports car, and his daughter is dating some freak with a sports car, you get a ticket...<BR>Welcome to the LEGAL system, ain't no JUSTICE to it!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000005||FLASHY||09-23-2001||03:36 AM||||That sucks man! From what I heard, Deerfoot WAS at one point restricted to RCMP control only and therefore photo-radar was not permitted BUT that didn't last for very long at all. There is still photo-radar and city cops roaming around there. Good luck though.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flash_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||1
Z||000006||JayUSA77||09-23-2001||03:38 AM||||put it this way if you go to court and the cop shows up you lost. but if you go and he doenst show up your all good. However the explaining to the judge LOL it doesnt go that way sorry.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||09-23-2001||07:13 AM||||If you were doing 120 (what's that in the US?  About 70?), you were illegal.  It doesn't matter that the rest of the traffic was doing the same speed or that it's usual to go that fast in that area.  Sounds like he was being a prick, but it also sounds like he was correct in giving you the ticket.  Unless you're going to lose your drivers license over this (doesn't sound like it), I'd just pay the ticket and forget about it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||09-23-2001||01:08 PM||||you could do what i did for BS ticket. Go to the bank and buy that amount in change, i got pennies. Take them to courthouse and pay your fine. Still cost you the money, but really pisses them off. Took 3 people a couple hours to count mine, Haha. I even felt good afterwards. You ought to heard what i told them when they called me at home asking for donations to Police Assn.||||reg||1
