Z||000010||Mach10||09-23-2001||10:44 PM||||Roger: We have some obscure law stating that you don't have to consider pennies legal tender in amounts over $2.00. something about undue hardship in counting/carrying them.<BR>don't see anything about Nickels though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Just make sure you count CLOSELY, or they may try and nail you with fraud  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||JayUSA77||09-24-2001||12:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>you could do what i did for BS ticket. Go to the bank and buy that amount in change, i got pennies. Take them to courthouse and pay your fine. Still cost you the money, but really pisses them off. Took 3 people a couple hours to count mine, Haha. I even felt good afterwards. You ought to heard what i told them when they called me at home asking for donations to Police Assn.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> i laughed for 5 min and im forever in your debt. Im doing that for my next speeding ticket fine 270 bucks. <BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000012||Butter||09-24-2001||01:24 PM||||How did the cop know you were doing the speed he wrote down on the ticket.  The last time I ask a TN Trooper he said the radar they had could not clock anyone going in the same direction and their policy in such a case was to fiscally clock them which requires a certain amount of distance to be legit.  The last undercover cop that stopped me for speeding fed me a line of BS and I was nice and only TOLD him one thing. "Sounds like you need to get a State Trooper hear for this."  He wound up letting me go since he was doing over 15 mph over the limit without any blue lights on.  I and my father with me thought he wanted to race and there was no traffic ahead so I blowed by a GT Mustang's a$$.  He pulled in my lane as, if he could, and faded away in my mirror.  He was also out of his jurisdiction.  Fight it!||||reg||1
Z||000013||LZeitgeist||09-24-2001||02:08 PM||||Ummmmm... if the guy is going 70mph, and the cop is going 70mph and is just able to merge behind him, seems like the cop could be pretty dang sure they were both doing 70 mph... I don't see the grey area here. <P>The cop still sounds like he was being a prick, though.||||reg||1
Z||000014||artherd||09-24-2001||10:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>If you were doing 120 (what's that in the US?  About 70?), you were illegal.  It doesn't matter that the rest of the traffic was doing the same speed </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sure does in the US.  "Basic Speed Law" means that if everyone in both lanes is doing 120MPH, then you have to also, or else you can actually be ticketed FOR going the speed limit, as you're a huge traffic hazard at 65MHP (or a closing speed of 55 with traffic....)<P>Anyway, it's gotta be my favourite law :")<P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000015||Brandon86SE||09-25-2001||12:03 AM||||Alright, update:  I found out about the jurisdiction thing for sure.  My best friends dad is an RCMP officer who used to be stationed in Airdrie, and he said that the city cops to have the right to give tickets on those roads, but technically it is up to the RCMP to patrol them.  However, he also said it was a BS ticket, and to take it to the magistrate, which was my plan!<P>*Still venting*<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000016||Monkeyman||09-25-2001||05:10 AM||||artherd--Sorry, but it is never legal for a civilian to exceed the speed limit.  If you're traveling slower then the posted speed limit, you can be ticketed, but you can never be ticketed for going the speed limit.  If I ever get a  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> ticket for going the speed limit (not much of a chance I'll be caught doing the right speed, though), I'll fight it to the Supreme Court.  I had a friend who was speeding to get his pregnant wife to the hospital.  He got a ticket and it stuck.||||reg||1
Z||000017||rogergarrison||09-25-2001||01:00 PM||||may have to check with local policys. but i checked with my lawyer and he told me that they had to accept it because it was 'legal tender for all debts, private and public'. at least in that jurastiction. And you know what, when I go thru same town now, they dont even look my way!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||grinthock||09-25-2001||05:40 PM||||A Couple comments<P>First:  In Canada, you do not have to accept any coins if their quantity exceeds that of ONE roll, you can provide them however in ROLLS (so a $300 ticket would be 600 rolls of pennies!).  So anything over 50 cents in pennies they can deny that as a valid method of payment, and that's FEDERAL statue.<P>Second:  He was correct to give you a speeding ticket.  BUT, he's being an ass, it's obvious you were acting in the best interests of all drivers on the road.  Had you slowed down, you would have caused a hazard moving into the centre lane, basically explain to the magistrate that you sped up to AVOID the police car that was merging into the lane YOU were in, and had you NOT sped up and quickly changed lanes to the left, he would have HIT you!<P>Basically turn it back on him.  And say you were driving defenseivly, YES you were speeding, but had you not sped up to avoid the officer, you would have caused an accident.  Had the officer merged properly and not at the last moment, none of this would have happened.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Brandon86SE||10-21-2001||05:01 PM||||Alright everyone, wish me luck, I go in to talk to the magistrate tomorrow morning after my Advanced Calculus final exam!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  (At least I like calculus.......)<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000020||Brian87egotrip||10-21-2001||09:33 PM||||Good Luck!<P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000021||Brandon86SE||10-22-2001||05:54 PM||||So I went to talk to the Justice of the Peace today.  I just told him my story on what happened, and he offered me two options.<P>1 - I could pay the full $82 and get no demerits.<P>2 - I could get bumped down to 110 ($54) and get 2 demerits.<P>Since I am strapped for cash, and don't plan on getting any more tickets (this has been the first in over 3 years of driving), I went for the reduction.  He guaranteed me that 2 demerits would not affect my insurance, so it's all good.  Plus I got a month extension to pay.  I'm in a pretty good mood now.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But I gotta get back to studying AC circuits for my final tomorrow.<P>Brandon||||reg||14
